{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 756150,
  "courseSlug": "the-complete-guide-to-angular-2",
  "courseTitle": "Angular - The Complete Guide",
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "44116000",
      "title": "Using Angular's Dependency Injection Mechanism",
      "lectureOrder": 179,
      "videoOrder": 171,
      "sourceHash": "befcff07d4926b4204edfcd9b5b56635f6a38e551497839ad5d347bfb833e10b",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.75,
          "end": 4.276,
          "en": "Angular has this built-in feature",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.276,
          "end": 7.05,
          "en": "called Dependency Injection, which in the end means",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 7.05,
          "end": 12.05,
          "en": "that Components, Directives and Services can request values,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 13.47,
          "end": 15.99,
          "en": "dependencies they rely on,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 15.99,
          "end": 18.933,
          "en": "which are then provided by Angular.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 20.22,
          "end": 21.78,
          "en": "The idea is that you don't have",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 21.78,
          "end": 24.93,
          "en": "to create service instances yourself,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 24.93,
          "end": 27.09,
          "en": "though, as you will see later,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 27.09,
          "end": 29.4,
          "en": "Angular's Dependency Injection mechanism",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 29.4,
          "end": 32.13,
          "en": "is actually not limited to services,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 32.13,
          "end": 34.95,
          "en": "but it's the most common type of value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 34.95,
          "end": 37.89,
          "en": "that is requested and injected.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 37.89,
          "end": 41.25,
          "en": "So the idea is that you don't have to create those values,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 41.25,
          "end": 43.56,
          "en": "those services on your own,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 43.56,
          "end": 46.83,
          "en": "but that instead you request them in your Components,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 46.83,
          "end": 49.83,
          "en": "Directives and Services from Angular,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 49.83,
          "end": 53.13,
          "en": "and then Angular creates those values,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 53.13,
          "end": 56.4,
          "en": "those service class instances, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 56.4,
          "end": 61.4,
          "en": "and passes them to your Components, Directives and Services.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 61.65,
          "end": 66.51,
          "en": "And for that, Angular uses multiple injectors,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 66.51,
          "end": 71.51,
          "en": "which it manages, where you can register your services,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 71.82,
          "end": 76.05,
          "en": "and I'll get back to that later, how you can register things",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 76.05,
          "end": 79.65,
          "en": "with these injectors, and your Components, Directives",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 79.65,
          "end": 84.03,
          "en": "or Services in the end, then when they request a dependency,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 84.03,
          "end": 86.25,
          "en": "go through these injectors",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 86.25,
          "end": 90.6,
          "en": "and see if the dependency can be fetched from there,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 90.6,
          "end": 94.59,
          "en": "if Angular is able to provide the requested service class",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 94.59,
          "end": 96.57,
          "en": "with one of its injectors.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 96.57,
          "end": 100.56,
          "en": "But again, I'll get back to those injectors later.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 100.56,
          "end": 103.11,
          "en": "For the moment, it's just important to understand",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 103.11,
          "end": 104.64,
          "en": "that the idea is not",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 104.64,
          "end": 108.96000000000001,
          "en": "that you create instances like this one here on your own,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 108.96000000000001,
          "end": 111.45,
          "en": "but that you instead use Angular for that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 111.45,
          "end": 113.78999999999999,
          "en": "And you saw that earlier in the course already.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 113.78999999999999,
          "end": 116.16,
          "en": "Of course, it's just really important",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 116.16,
          "end": 118.053,
          "en": "to understand this concept.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 119.28,
          "end": 123.3,
          "en": "Therefore, what you would do here in the NewTaskComponent",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 123.3,
          "end": 127.5,
          "en": "is instead of instantiating this tasksService on your own,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 127.5,
          "end": 131.28,
          "en": "you would request it as a dependency by specifying it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 131.28,
          "end": 134.73,
          "en": "as a parameter here in the constructor.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 134.73,
          "end": 139.2,
          "en": "So here we could specify the tService parameter,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 139.2,
          "end": 140.7,
          "en": "the name doesn't matter,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 140.7,
          "end": 143.85,
          "en": "which should be of type tasksService,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 143.85,
          "end": 148.38,
          "en": "and the type does matter because Angular's Compiler will,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 148.38,
          "end": 150.69,
          "en": "in the end, pick up that type",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 150.69,
          "end": 153.54,
          "en": "and understand that you're requesting a dependency",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 153.54,
          "end": 156.24,
          "en": "of that type here, and it will then kick off",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 156.24,
          "end": 158.34,
          "en": "that dependency injection mechanism",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 158.34,
          "end": 161.46,
          "en": "because of this type in this constructor here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 161.46,
          "end": 163.773,
          "en": "So this type here is important.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 165.42000000000002,
          "end": 168,
          "en": "And then here we could set our tasksService",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 168,
          "end": 171.06,
          "en": "to this tService parameter value,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 171.06,
          "end": 173.67000000000002,
          "en": "so to this instance of the tasksService",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 173.67000000000002,
          "end": 175.953,
          "en": "that has been provided by Angular.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 176.97,
          "end": 180.75,
          "en": "And it is Angular that will create and provide that instance",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 180.75,
          "end": 184.92,
          "en": "because these Component classes, just like Directive classes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 184.92,
          "end": 188.31,
          "en": "or Service classes, are not instantiated",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 188.31,
          "end": 190.98,
          "en": "by us anywhere in our code,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 190.98,
          "end": 193.74,
          "en": "instead, Angular will do that behind the scenes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 193.74,
          "end": 196.98,
          "en": "So it's Angular's job to provide the values",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 196.98,
          "end": 199.743,
          "en": "for the parameters in the constructor function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 201.72,
          "end": 205.38,
          "en": "Now, this is the longest possible way of writing this code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 205.38,
          "end": 210.24,
          "en": "A shorter way would be to use a TypeScript shortcut",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 210.24,
          "end": 213.21,
          "en": "and add the private or public keyword",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 213.21,
          "end": 215.47,
          "en": "in front of this parameter here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 216.66,
          "end": 219.32999999999998,
          "en": "so that TypeScript would automatically go ahead",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 219.32999999999998,
          "end": 223.77,
          "en": "and create a property with the same name for this class.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 223.77,
          "end": 226.95,
          "en": "That's simply a convenient feature offered by TypeScript.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 226.95,
          "end": 228.54,
          "en": "And therefore, we could then get rid",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 228.54,
          "end": 230.883,
          "en": "of this extra property here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 232.41,
          "end": 235.05,
          "en": "and instead rename this here to tasksService",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 235.05,
          "end": 236.52,
          "en": "and get rid of this code,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 236.52,
          "end": 240.333,
          "en": "and therefore have a shorter way of requesting a service.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 242.04,
          "end": 243.9,
          "en": "By the way, whether you use private",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 243.9,
          "end": 246.96,
          "en": "or public here isn't too important.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 246.96,
          "end": 249.93,
          "en": "The main difference here is that private properties",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 249.93,
          "end": 252.99,
          "en": "are not accessible from inside the template,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 252.99,
          "end": 257.43,
          "en": "whereas public properties are, and that might matter",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 257.43,
          "end": 259.47,
          "en": "because you might wanna make sure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 259.47,
          "end": 261.39,
          "en": "that from inside the template,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 261.39,
          "end": 264.24,
          "en": "you are not accidentally directly interacting",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 264.24,
          "end": 267.39,
          "en": "with the service, but that you instead only use it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 267.39,
          "end": 269.523,
          "en": "from inside your component class.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 270.66,
          "end": 274.59000000000003,
          "en": "So with that done, finally we're injecting the service such",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 274.59000000000003,
          "end": 277.56,
          "en": "that we'll be operating on one shared instance",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 277.56,
          "end": 279.423,
          "en": "across the entire application.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 280.32,
          "end": 283.02,
          "en": "Now, of course, we also want to access the service",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 283.02,
          "end": 285.54,
          "en": "from inside the tasks-list.component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 285.54,
          "end": 288.303,
          "en": "to get hold of our tasks there,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 289.14,
          "end": 291.84000000000003,
          "en": "and that's what we'll take care of in the next lecture.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 291.84000000000003,
          "end": 294.84000000000003,
          "en": "And there, I'll also show you another way",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 294.84000000000003,
          "end": 297.78,
          "en": "of injecting values into Components",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 297.78,
          "end": 299.823,
          "en": "or other things in Angular.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
